Ladybird defers the parser’s fragment scroll until blocking stylesheets
settle. Blink’s ElementFragmentAnchor::Invoke checks rendering readiness
and can revisit the target until load completes. WebKit maintains the
target in LocalFrameView::maintainScrollPositionAtAnchor and scrolls to
it in LocalFrameView::scrollToAnchor. Gecko’s PresShell::ScrollToAnchor
revisits the last anchor at its recorded scroll position.

Chrome 158.0.8127.36, Firefox 151.0, and WebKit 26.5 brought FFmpeg’s
named anchor and its adjacent line number into view. All three also
aligned the target after a delayed stylesheet moved it, including when
DOMContentLoaded had scrolled a nested box first.
